### Bug Scenario and Root Cause

The bug scenario involves generating a Lighthouse report using headless Chrome, which does not support network throttling. This results in a warning message at the top of the report indicating that the performance numbers may not be accurate for mobile connections. The warning is placed prominently to ensure visibility, as performance-related audits are present in multiple categories.

### Bug Location and Analysis

The issue is related to the rendering of the report header in the `lighthouse-core/report/v2/renderer/report-renderer.js` file. The warning message needs to be added to the report header to inform users about the potential inaccuracies in performance metrics when using headless Chrome.

### Patches

To fix the issue, we need to modify the `_renderReportHeader` method to include the warning message when the report is generated using headless Chrome.

